    <item>
      <title>Unity Tools</title>
      <link>https://torres-xyz.github.io/portfolioblog/posts/unity_tools/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 10 Jan 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://torres-xyz.github.io/portfolioblog/posts/unity_tools/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;I&amp;rsquo;ve done some custom Unity tools for different projects and for different companies.&#xA;Here are some of them:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;timeline-editor&#34;&gt;Timeline Editor&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;https://torres-xyz.github.io/portfolioblog/images/unity_tool_timeline.png&#34; alt=&#34;Fakedoor Timeline&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This timeline editor allows you to &lt;strong&gt;schedule&lt;/strong&gt; different types of &lt;strong&gt;events&lt;/strong&gt; in a Unity scene.&#xA;If you create a &lt;em&gt;Linear&lt;/em&gt; timeline, the script will wait for each timeline item to be finished&#xA;before starting the next one.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;If you create a &lt;em&gt;Parallel&lt;/em&gt; timeline, the script will play all timeline items at once.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>C&#43;&#43; and Raylib</title>
      <link>https://torres-xyz.github.io/portfolioblog/posts/cpp_and_raylib/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 02 Jan 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://torres-xyz.github.io/portfolioblog/posts/cpp_and_raylib/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;I have been learning &lt;strong&gt;C++&lt;/strong&gt; for about a year now. I started by reading almost the entirety&#xA;of &lt;a href=&#34;https://learncpp.com/&#34;&gt;learncpp.com&lt;/a&gt;, and then I began developing some small games using &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.raylib.com/&#34;&gt;Raylib&lt;/a&gt;,&#xA;and it was great fun. At least until I hit the &lt;strong&gt;CMake&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;ldquo;wall&amp;rdquo;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I have since read &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.packtpub.com/en-us/product/minimal-cmake-9781835080658&#34;&gt;Minimal CMake&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.packtpub.com/en-us/product/modern-cmake-for-c-9781805123361&#34;&gt;Modern CMake for C++&lt;/a&gt;.&#xA;&lt;strong&gt;CMake&lt;/strong&gt; makes sense now, and I have come to enjoy it.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;With these skills I am now developing a simple card game with &lt;strong&gt;C++&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;Raylib&lt;/strong&gt;,&#xA;as well as &lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/ocornut/imgui&#34;&gt;Dear Imgui&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/catchorg/Catch2&#34;&gt;catch2&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Raylib</title>
      <link>https://torres-xyz.github.io/portfolioblog/posts/raylib/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 11 Sep 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://torres-xyz.github.io/portfolioblog/posts/raylib/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Yesterday I started playing around with the raylib library. It was surprisingly easy to&#xA;get started with and use.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I used &amp;lsquo;vcpkg&amp;rsquo; to install raylib and set up and the dependencies and environments and&#xA;quickly completed a small Pong tutorial.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;https://torres-xyz.github.io/portfolioblog/images/raylib/raylib-pong-1.webp&#34; alt=&#34;&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I plan on expanding it in the future, and add menus and sound effects. I&amp;rsquo;ll keep&#xA;posting updates here.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Visual Studio Code Snippets</title>
      <link>https://torres-xyz.github.io/portfolioblog/posts/visual_studio_snippets/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 06 Aug 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://torres-xyz.github.io/portfolioblog/posts/visual_studio_snippets/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Pasting my VS Code Snippets here for quick reference:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;serializefield-snippet&#34;&gt;SerializeField Snippet&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Type &lt;code&gt;sfield&lt;/code&gt; to get &lt;code&gt;[SerializeField] private&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;?xml version=&amp;quot;1.0&amp;quot; encoding=&amp;quot;utf-8&amp;quot;?&amp;gt;&#xA;&amp;lt;CodeSnippets xmlns=&amp;quot;http://schemas.microsoft.com/VisualStudio/2005/CodeSnippet&amp;quot;&amp;gt;&#xA;&#x9;&amp;lt;CodeSnippet Format=&amp;quot;1.0.0&amp;quot;&amp;gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&amp;lt;Header&amp;gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&amp;lt;Title&amp;gt;[SerializeField]&amp;lt;/Title&amp;gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&amp;lt;Author&amp;gt;Francisco Torres&amp;lt;/Author&amp;gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&amp;lt;Shortcut&amp;gt;sfield&amp;lt;/Shortcut&amp;gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&amp;lt;/Header&amp;gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&amp;lt;Snippet&amp;gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&amp;lt;Code Language=&amp;quot;CSharp&amp;quot;&amp;gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&amp;lt;![CDATA[[SerializeField] private $Type$;$end$]]&amp;gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&amp;lt;/Code&amp;gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&amp;lt;Declarations&amp;gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&amp;lt;Literal&amp;gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&amp;lt;ID&amp;gt;Type&amp;lt;/ID&amp;gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&amp;lt;ToolTip&amp;gt;Variable type&amp;lt;/ToolTip&amp;gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&amp;lt;Default&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/Default&amp;gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&amp;lt;/Literal&amp;gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&amp;lt;/Declarations&amp;gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&amp;lt;/Snippet&amp;gt;&#xA;&#x9;&amp;lt;/CodeSnippet&amp;gt;&#xA;&amp;lt;/CodeSnippets&amp;gt;&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;header-snippet&#34;&gt;Header Snippet&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Type &lt;code&gt;header&lt;/code&gt; to get &lt;code&gt;[Header(&amp;quot; &amp;quot;)]&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;?xml version=&amp;quot;1.0&amp;quot; encoding=&amp;quot;utf-8&amp;quot;?&amp;gt;&#xA;&amp;lt;CodeSnippets xmlns=&amp;quot;http://schemas.microsoft.com/VisualStudio/2005/CodeSnippet&amp;quot;&amp;gt;&#xA;&#x9;&amp;lt;CodeSnippet Format=&amp;quot;1.0.0&amp;quot;&amp;gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&amp;lt;Header&amp;gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&amp;lt;Title&amp;gt;Header Attribute&amp;lt;/Title&amp;gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&amp;lt;Author&amp;gt;Francisco Torres&amp;lt;/Author&amp;gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&amp;lt;Shortcut&amp;gt;header&amp;lt;/Shortcut&amp;gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&amp;lt;/Header&amp;gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&amp;lt;Snippet&amp;gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&amp;lt;Code Language=&amp;quot;CSharp&amp;quot;&amp;gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&amp;lt;![CDATA[[Header(&amp;quot;$Text$&amp;quot;)]$end$]]&amp;gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&amp;lt;/Code&amp;gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&amp;lt;Declarations&amp;gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&amp;lt;Literal&amp;gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&amp;lt;ID&amp;gt;Text&amp;lt;/ID&amp;gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&amp;lt;ToolTip&amp;gt;Use this PropertyAttribute to add a header above some fields in the Inspector.&amp;lt;/ToolTip&amp;gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&amp;lt;Default&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/Default&amp;gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&amp;lt;/Literal&amp;gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&amp;lt;/Declarations&amp;gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&amp;lt;/Snippet&amp;gt;&#xA;&#x9;&amp;lt;/CodeSnippet&amp;gt;&#xA;&amp;lt;/CodeSnippets&amp;gt;&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;debuglog-snippet&#34;&gt;DebugLog Snippet&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Type &lt;code&gt;log&lt;/code&gt; to get &lt;code&gt;Debug.Log($&amp;quot; &amp;quot;);&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Fakedoor</title>
